jobs_results.description:
Para un importante cliente del sector seguros en Madrid, buscamos Experto en Redes LAN/ WAN / SDWAN, el trabajo es 100% remoto, ofrecemos contrato indefinido con nosotros.

Services:
• Defining, advertising and ensuring to deliver of sustainable, robust and secured solutions. In close collaboration with Group Security, CTO and One Network Program, the service will propose solutions at the right cost and bring business value to support the corporate business and lines of business strategies;
• Contributing and supporting a medium to long term product evolution and continuous product improvement;
• Managing the advisory, selection, design, secure build & integration for the products in scope;
• Facilitating communications and interactions between functional groups, AXA IT Services, strategic partners and vendors;
• Ensuring QOS delivery and supporting of solutions;
• Providing high expertise support on products and services.

Deliverables:
• Service will require expertise in driving... large architecture, standardization & transformation initiatives.
• Designing of the wireless and wired standard for our offices for any onsite users; smaller project related to Wireless and LAN;
• Designing and industrialize large scale wireless infrastructure and associated LAN;
• Service will require an implementation and management of other LAN, Wireless and SDWAN solutions; current standard is mostly based on Cisco products for LAN, Wireless and NAC with an ongoing vendor selection.

Expertise:
• Expertise in remote sites design patterns, Security solutions & IT infrastructure best practices;
• Expertise in managing LAN, Wireless and WAN infrastructure;
• Expertise about all technologies deployed in LAN, WAN, and SDWAN global environments;
• Expertise in DC Network, Cloud, Network Security products, SASE, VPN (Cisco, F5), Firewalling (Checkpoint, Palo Alto, Cisco, Algosec), Web gateways (McAfee), Segmentation technologies and identity services;
• Service will require an University degree (engineer profile) with senior expertise in Network Domain in an international and Matrix organization;
• Understanding of today’s Network and infrastructure challenges and trends, mostly at Infrastructure and Technical levels;
• Expertise in implementing Network project requirements, ensuring business readiness and providing business as usual support in a complex multi-tenanted environment;
• Establishing and demonstrably productive technical relationships with major IT vendors;
• Delivering high quality and ability to work in tight planning;
• Gathering, combining and analyzing business and technical requirements from critical constituents. Recommend appropriate technological designs and solutions that align with business requirements, the company’s technical strategy and which provides the most efficient and cost-effective solution;
• Expertise of automation and network management platforms;
• Service will require ability to work in a multi-cultural, and challenging global environment;
• Building effective networks within the organisation.

Se requiere ingles avanzado

